---
description: "Security and secrets hygiene for Next.js apps."
globs:
  - "lib/env.ts"
  - "lib/auth/**/*.ts"
  - "app/api/**/*.ts"
  - "**/.env*"
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow root `AGENTS.md`.

Security checklist:

- Validate all external input with Zod.
- Never invent or commit secrets; use `.env.local` and deployment secrets.
- Prefer server-only modules for tokens and database clients.
- Avoid leaking stack traces or secrets in client responses.
- Do not disable auth checks to "just make it work".
